From 5f96e9827cbee3a0301ad9f819d922e05ec50501 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:20:48 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] ASoC: samsung: abox: build the ABOX core on 6.18

Forward-port the Exynos 9610 ABOX audio DSP core (firmware loader, IPC,
GIC, RDMA/WDMA PCMs, UAIF/DSIF/SPDY, effect, log/debug, failsafe) to the
6.18 kernel. Built in only (each component registers a platform driver).

Platform/ASoC API:
- RDMA/WDMA: snd_soc_platform -> snd_soc_component (pcm callbacks with the
  component argument, pcm_construct/pcm_destruct, snd_compress_ops with
  snd_compr_tstamp64); Samsung's get_hw_params compress op dropped.
- DAI: compress_new moved to snd_soc_dai_ops; symmetric_rate/_sample_bits,
  snd_soc_dai_get_widget_*(), clock provider DAIFMT names, const channel
  maps, two-argument snd_soc_component_read() (abox_cmpnt_read()).
- Samsung 4.14 ASoC additions kept local: snd_soc_dapm_connected_*_ep()
  (abox_dapm_connected_ep(), mainline is_connected_ep() semantics) and
  SND_SOC_DAPM_DEMUX_E.

Samsung-only kernel infrastructure:
- IOMMU: ABOX maps memory at fixed IOVAs, so it owns an unmanaged paging
  domain (iommu_paging_domain_alloc + iommu_attach_device) instead of the
  DMA API default domain; mappings use IOMMU_READ|IOMMU_WRITE (mainline
  exynos-iommu enforces access bits, the 4.14 prot 0 would deny access);
  exynos_sysmmu_control/tlb_invalidate dropped, iommu_set_fault_handler.
- Firmware DRAM (18 MiB) and private (8 MiB) areas come from a dedicated
  no-map "memory-region", memremap()ed write-combined, instead of
  dma_alloc_coherent() on the IOMMU device (which returns IOVAs on 6.18).
- The debug dump region (exynos,abox_rmem, no-map) is memremap()ed at
  probe instead of phys_to_virt().
- exynos_smc -> SMCCC (abox_smc), exynos_pmu_* -> PMU syscon regmap
  ("samsung,pmu-syscon"), 9610 offsets only.
- PM QoS: no Samsung QoS classes or AUD DVFS on 6.18; the ABOX CPU clock
  is set directly through the CMU (the legacy gear path); other classes
  only record requests. The AUD QoS notifier (SIFS counters on DVFS
  changes) is dropped with it.
- wakeup sources registered with wakeup_source_register(); panic notifier
  and pinctrl headers; FW_ACTION_UEVENT.
- The DSP log is no longer copied to /data from the kernel (set_fs gone);
  it stays in debugfs.
- An "ion" buffer type falls back to DMA buffers (no ION on 6.18).

Not ported, behind Kconfig options that depend on BROKEN, with inline
stubs: VSS voice path (modem shared memory, plan M11), Bluetooth SCO via
the WLBT mailbox (A2DP uses BlueZ, ADR-0008), ION MMAP data fds. The dump
card is optional (SND_SOC_SAMSUNG_ABOX_DUMP). IPC bundle views are sized
instead of zero-length arrays (same layout).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I92d9df5930b993cf68aeb4f49830cd0380f954ed
